================================================================================
MODEL OVERVIEW
================================================================================

MODEL: Windspeed (WS) Sector-Level Uncertainty Model (v3)
---------------------------------------------------------
Target: Signed relative windspeed deviation between cross-prediction and actual
Formula: e = (WS_predicted - WS_actual) / WS_actual
Level: Sector (12 sectors per pair)
Distribution: Student-t (robust to outliers)

Key features:
- Signed errors (captures over/under prediction direction)
- Student-t distribution handles heavy tails via learned ν parameter
- Provides ± confidence intervals for industry communication

Model structure:
    e ~ StudentT(ν, μ=0, σ)

    log(σ) = log_σ₀ + Σ(γᵢ × zᵢ) + pair_effect

    Where:
    - ν = degrees of freedom (learned from data, ν ≈ 25)
    - log_σ₀ = baseline log-sigma
    - γᵢ = effect of each driver (HalfNormal prior, always positive)
    - zᵢ = standardized (z-scored) driver values
    - pair_effect = random effect for each pair

