================================================================================
PRACTICAL USAGE
================================================================================

CONFIDENCE INTERVAL CALCULATION
-------------------------------
For a predicted σ, calculate confidence intervals using Student-t distribution:

    CI = ± t_critical(ν, confidence) × σ

For ν ≈ 25:
    50% CI: ± 0.685 × σ
    68% CI: ± 1.014 × σ
    90% CI: ± 1.708 × σ
    95% CI: ± 2.060 × σ
    99% CI: ± 2.787 × σ

Example:
    If model predicts σ = 10% for a sector:
    95% CI = ± 2.06 × 10% = ± 20.6%

    Interpretation: "There is 95% confidence the actual windspeed error
    for this sector is within ±20.6%"


DEPLOYMENT CONSIDERATIONS
-------------------------
1. Sample shortfall features use training data scaling
   - Consider using ws_shortfall as proxy (always available, same scale)

2. New masts not in training will use baseline σ + feature effects only
   - No pair-specific random effect available

3. Model assumes similar data quality to training set
   - Excluded masts had suspected measurement issues


================================================================================
INPUT DATA REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

For each sector to be evaluated, provide:

PAIR-LEVEL COLUMNS:
- pair_id: Unique identifier (e.g., "SiteA__SiteB")
- dz: Height difference in meters (WTG - MM)
- distance_m: Distance between sites in meters
- distance_A: Lower acceptable distance bound
- distance_B: Upper acceptable distance bound

SECTOR-LEVEL COLUMNS:
- sector_name: N, NNE, ENE, E, ESE, SSE, S, SSW, WSW, W, WNW, NNW
- Mean_windspeed_self: Measured windspeed at MM location
- overall_speedup_WTG_factor: Speedup at WTG location
- overall_speedup_MM_factor: Speedup at MM location
- RIX_avg_0.3_sector: Average terrain severity
- dRIX_0.3_sector: Terrain severity difference
- d_turning_deg: Wind deflection angle
- flip_fraction_weighted_by_predicted_power: Energy flip fraction
- weight_energy_predicted: Energy weight per sector
- Sample_count_pred: Sample count per sector


